//@ run-pass
//@ requires: madaros
// Task 4 Step 5/6: adversarial chain-verification suite. Reuses the same
// root/intermediate/leaf fixtures as x509_chain_verify_positive.sio for
// cases (a)-(d) (each mutates exactly one input: the timestamp passed to
// x509_verify_chain, a signature byte, or the hostname), plus two
// dedicated fixtures for (e) and (f) that need a structurally different
// chain. Every case asserts the EXACT expected CHAIN_ERR_* constant.
//
// Case (d) asserts "wrong hostname -> CHAIN_ERR_HOSTNAME_MISMATCH". The
// SAN `value_len`-loss compiler defect that once made this indistinguishable
// from a matching hostname (Madaros losing `san_entries[i].value_len`
// across `x509_parse_certificate`'s own return) was fixed in commit
// 1168f99a3, earlier on this plan -- `x509_verify_hostname` now exercises
// its real match/mismatch logic here, not just the constant.
//
// Fixtures (e)/(f) generated via openssl the same way as
// x509_chain_verify_positive.sio's root/inter/leaf (see that file's header
// for the exact commands); (e) is root -> inter1[pathlen:0] -> inter2[CA:true]
// -> leaf (inter1 forbids any CA below it, and inter2 is one), (f) is
// root -> inter[CA:false] -> leaf (inter is not a CA at all).

